{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Description rewritten and re-based on `origin/main` `403719c01ce`. The sweep found one inverted premise, four unusable counts, an unsatisfiable AC, and an unenumerated file.\n\n**1. The CHANGELOG half was written against a pre-v0.14.0 tree.** The old plan directed both commits' entries to `[Unreleased]`. Verified ancestry instead of trusting it:\n\n| commit | v0.13.0 | v0.13.1 | v0.14.0 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `334ee94` \"Remove scheduled public deprecations\" | no | no | **ancestor** |\n| `81da792` \"Retire the HLC rollback switch\" | no | no | **ancestor** |\n\nBoth shipped in 0.14.0 (released 2026-10-30). Filing them as unreleased would have published a changelog claiming shipped work is pending. `334ee94`'s two bullets are currently misfiled one release *too early*, under `[0.13.0]`; they move forward to `[0.14.0]`, not into `[Unreleased]`. Only this epic's own in-flight work belongs in `[Unreleased]`.\n\n**2. All four hardcoded counts were wrong, and hardcoding any count is itself the defect.** Plan said 104 canonical / 165 rows / 64 missing / 227 target. Measured: 105 / 109 / 68 / 177. But correcting the numbers would not fix the AC — `cb2b` and `b939` both land ahead of this story and both change the name set (`b939` removes two). Any literal is stale before implementation starts. AC1 now derives both sides and asserts no total; the planned test already did this correctly, so only the AC text was at fault.\n\n**3. AC3 was unsatisfiable.** It required `grep -n 'force_close\\|REBAR_HLC' CHANGELOG.md` to return only line numbers `< 99`. Two hits can never satisfy that: `:620` is a historical cross-reference and `:1342` is the 2025 entry recording `force_close`'s introduction. Neither is in scope to move, and nothing this story does can renumber them below 99. AC3 now asserts section membership.\n\n**4. `test_canary_bridge_heldout.py:122` was not in the plan's file list.** It sets `REBAR_CANARY_HEARTBEAT_SOURCE` to `\"status\"`, not `\"github-api\"`, so a `github-api`-shaped search missed it — but AC2's alternation matches the key name, so AC2 would have failed at the end with the file untouched. Now enumerated in the Approach.\n\n**Citation drift fixed (measured on `403719c01ce`):**\n\n| plan said | actual |\n|---|---|\n| `render` `:489-497` | `:400` |\n| MCP union — unlocated | `:406-409` |\n| rollback source — unlocated | `canary_bridge.py:140-143`, `:687` |\n| workflow — unlocated | `:28`, `:34`, `:54`, `:134` |\n| `test_canary_bridge.py` — unlocated | `:71` |\n| heldout — 1 site | `:74`, `:122`, `:145`, `:168` |\n| `test_canary_status_refs_heldout.py` — unlocated | `:133` |\n| `_canonical_env_name` — unlocated | `_config_sources.py:289` |\n| `[Unreleased]`/`[0.14.0]` — unlocated | `:11` / `:13` (`### Changed` `:15`) |\n\n**Verified sound — do not \"fix\" these.** The decision to leave `detect_config.py:63-81` alone is correct and now carries its reason (no marker path for dozens of derived names). Keeping `_check_github_heartbeat` for the `NEVER_RUN` bootstrap is required by ADR 0094 `:81-82`. `REBAR_CANARY_HEARTBEAT_SOURCE` genuinely has no `env_var::` baseline row, so the mechanism ratchet is unaffected. `tests/unit/test_env_registry_helper_coverage.py` is genuinely unaffected.\n\nThis is the fourth of four remaining stories in the epic to carry an acceptance criterion that could not certify its own work. Standing rule for the rest: run every AC verbatim before implementing and record its pre-state in the AC text. An AC whose current result is unknown is not a criterion."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793424565549277985,"uuid":"9fd23caf-c157-4b02-aaa7-cd6dd2d5628f"}